  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Salim Marshal vs Chellanam Grama Panchayat on 21 August, 2024 Wp(C) No. 13432 Of 2024 1 2024:Ker:63829 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr.Justice Mohammed Nias C.P. Wednesday, The 21St Day Of August 2024 / 30Th Sravana, 1946 Wp(C) No. 13432 Of 2024 Petitioner: Salim Marshal, Aged 73 Years Son Of A.X. Marshal, Arackal House, Ndakkadavu, Andikkadavu P.O., Kochi, Ernakulam District, Pin - 682008 By Advs. S.Vinod Bhat Anagha Lakshmy Raman V.Namitha Greeshma Chandrika.R Respondents: 1 Chellanam Grama Panchayat, Andikadavu P.O., Kandakkadavu, Ernakulam Represented By Its Secretary, Pin - 682008 2 The Secretary, Chellanam Grama Panchayat, Andikadavu P.O., Kandakkadavu, Ernakulam, Pin - 682008 3 Addl.R3.Health Inspector, Family Welfare Division, Chellanam, Ernakulam District, Pin - 682008 Salim Marshal vs Chellanam Grama Panchayat on 21 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/127801091/ 1 4 Addl. R4.Kerala State Pollution Control Board, Gandhi Nagar,Ernakulam, Represented By Chief Environmental Engineer. Wp(C) No. 13432 Of 2024 2 2024:Ker:63829 (Additional R3 And R4 Are Impleaded As Per Order Dated 11.04.2024 In I.A.1/2024) By Advs. Dinesh R.Shenoy - Sc Silesh S. Prabhu Jomol Pius Vishakha J. Sri . T.Naveen Sc, Kerala State Pollution Control Board , Smt. Devi Shri R - Gp This Writ Petition (Civil) Having Been Finally Heard On 21.08.2024, The Court On The Same Day Delivered The Following: Wp(C) No. 13432 Of 2024 3 2024:Ker:63829 Mohammed Nias C.P., J. ============================= W.P.(C.) No. 13432 of 2024 ============================== Dated this the 21st day of August, 2024 Judgment",
    "facts": "The petitioner challenges Ext.P11 notice issued by the Panchayat refusing the renewal of the licence to run a prawn peeling shed on account of the alleged water pollution. Thereafter, the petitioner was served with Ext.P12 by the Pollution Control Board on 09.05.2024. Accordingly, there will be a direction to the Pollution Control Board to take a decision on Ext.P15 application for consent to operate.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
